```

This code defines a method on the contract class that is called every time the Pex engine executes a test case on this class. It checks that the IndexOf and LastIndexOf methods return the expected values and that Contains method returns the expected value after removing the element x. 

## Checking pre-conditions
The `AssumePrecondition.IsTrue` method tells Pex that a true condition is required to continue with the testing. If it's not met, Pex will produce an empty test case and skip it.

## Observing intermediate values
The `PexObserve` class allows Pex to show temporary values for verification.

## Assertions
Assertions are used to guarantee the correctness of the code. They are used to validate the results of the test cases. The `Debug.Assert` method in C# allows you to check and ensure certain conditions.

## Conclusion
The contract-based approach helps improve code correctness and efficiency, by showing Pex the structure and behavior of a method, and helping it produce tests to verify those properties.--------------------		    Assert.IsTrue(New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount - 1);

	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ index of x in new array is lt minus 1 
		    Assert.IsTrue(New_arrListIndexOfX < Old_arrListIndexOfX);

	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ last index of x in new array is leq minus 1 
		    Assert.IsTrue(New_arrListLastIndexOfX <= Old_arrListLastIndexOfX);

	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ contains x in old array is false 
		    Assert.IsTrue(Old_arrListContainsX == false);

	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ contains x in new array is false 
		    Assert.IsTrue(New_arrListContainsX == false);

		    // The count of list should be reduced by 1.
		    Assert.AreEqual(-1, New_arrListIndexOfX);
		    Assert.AreEqual(-1, New_arrListLastIndexOfX);
        }
    }
}
```

This test method is the first of two test methods that you can use to verify the Remove method, ensuring that the array list properly removes an item from the array list.

To run this contract test, you must first set the array list object and the specific index to be removed (x). Then, the test runs the Remove operation on the specified array list index for the object at the specified index, then checks if the Count has been reduced by one, and also checks if the other functions like IndexOf, LastIndexOf, and Contains have been updated correctly. If any check fails, the test will fail.--------------------